# Luminate schema reference

When writing or changing SQL that touches Luminate views, **consult the official docs** rather than inventing column names or semantics.

## Primary docs

- Market Share schema (views, columns, types, update cadence):
  https://docs.luminatedata.com/docs/market-share
- Docs index for related pages (dates, metadata, best practices, etc.):
  https://docs.luminatedata.com/llms.txt

Prefer fetching those URLs when unsure about a field. Related guides often needed here: Mapping Data, Reference Data, Fact Data Structure, Best Practices, Market IDs.

## Views this repo relies on

| View | Typical source | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `VW_WEEKLY_FACT_MARKET_SHARE_LEGACY_DS` | `LUMINATE_PROD_WMGONLY.EXTRACT_S` | Weekly market-share facts (legacy methodology) |
| `VW_BUSINESS_UNIT_DS` | `LUMINATE_PROD_WMGONLY.EXTRACT_S` | BU metadata (`BU_ID`, names, date ranges) |
| `VW_BUSINESS_UNIT_HIERARCHY_DS` | `LUMINATE_PROD_WMGONLY.EXTRACT_S` | Parent/child BU hierarchy + `LEVEL` |
| `VW_DATE_DS` | `LUMINATE_PROD.EXTRACT_S` | Chart weeks / calendar (`WEEKID`, `WEEK_END_DATE`, …) |

## Doc reminders that affect queries

- Cluster keys on market-share facts: `COUNTRY_CODE`, `WEEK_ID` — filter on these when possible
- Market-share views refresh daily, but that refresh window is only the current + most recently completed quarter — this limits which weeks are *updated*, not which weeks are *retained*; historical weeks can still be queried from the share
- BU / hierarchy / rights views use `START_DATE` / `END_DATE` validity windows — join as-of the week end date
- `WEEK_ID` is chart week in `YYYYWW` format
- NOTE: VW_WEEKLY_FACT_MARKET_SHARE_DS currently does not exist in the schema. Use VW_WEEKLY_FACT_MARKET_SHARE_LEGACY_DS instead.